    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7-qaDt",
      "title": "eth/066: Soneium Mainnet fee-vault recipient update (all four L2 vaults)",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1520,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **eth/066-soneium-fee-vault-recipient-update**: rotates the recipient of all four Soneium Mainnet (chainId 1868) L2 fee-vault predeploys (Sequencer/Base/L1/Operator) to the new Soneium fee recipient Safe `0x34ffF1A1CB3C054E9eD1BbD36883B14A66E6C260`, and lowers the minimum withdrawal amount **10 ETH → 5 ETH** on the three vaults that carry it (operator-approved; OperatorFeeVault's min stays 0).\n\n- Same `SetFeeVaultConfig` mechanism proven on Ink by eth/062 — **no template changes**: `OptimismPortal2.depositTransaction` from the L1PAO, whose alias (`0x6B1B…C4E3b`) is the Soneium L2 ProxyAdmin owner the setters authorize against (verified live). Vaults are on the post-Karst setter design (Seq/Base/L1 v1.6.1, Operator v1.1.1) — in-place config update, no upgrades.\n- Per-field skip-unchanged emits exactly **7 deposits** (150k gas each): 4× `setRecipient` + 3× `setMinWithdrawalAmount(5e18)`. Withdrawal networks (all L2) untouched.\n- The 5 ETH value doubles as the fix for a tooling constraint: TOML integers are int64-bounded (max ~9.22e18), so the live 10 ETH (1e19 wei) minimum could not be expressed as a bare TOML integer — 5 ETH can, keeping this PR task-only.\n- `OperatorFeeVault` previously cascaded into `BaseFeeVault`; it now pays the new recipient directly (net destination identical).\n- New recipient verified live: a 3-of-5 Safe deployed at the **same address on both L1 and Soneium L2** (canonical Safe v1.4.1 singletons, identical owner sets).\n\n## Ordering / nonces\n\nNumbered after eth/065 (#1515, now merged) and planned to execute after it. **No nonce coupling**: eth/065 is signed by the Foundation Operations Safe, so the nonce pins here (L1PAO 40 / FUS 66 / SC 64 — live, re-verified 2026-08-14) hold whether or not eth/065 has executed. They only break if another **L1PAO-signed** task lands first (re-verify before signing, per README/VALIDATION).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just simulate` on both nested paths (council + foundation): identical root safe tx hash; FUS/SC domain+message hashes recorded in VALIDATION.md, full task calldata injected verbatim from sim output and integrity-checked (7 deposits, each vault's field set exact).\n- CI-equivalent `just simulate-stack eth` green on the two-task stack (065 → 066): 065 reproduces its recorded hashes, and 066's hashes are identical stacked-after-065 vs standalone.\n- Manual anvil replay on a Soneium fork: all seven setters succeed at 45,406–45,656 gas (>3.2x headroom), exact expected end state, unrelated senders revert `ProxyAdminOwnedBase_NotProxyAdminOwner()`.\n\n## Signing gates (open items, tracked in README)\n\n1. Confirm the recipient Safe and the 5 ETH minimum with the Soneium chain operator out-of-band.\n2. Confirm whether a Maintenance Upgrade governance proposal is required (precedent: eth/062 needed one for the equivalent Ink change) and record the link before signing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-13T15:31:06Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-08-19T21:18:21Z",
      "additions": 479,
      "deletions": 1
